  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1:Quiet weather, temperatures warming to above\nnormal.\n\nA strong, broad area of surface high pressure will remain situated \nover the eastern US for much of the week. The center of the high \npasses overhead today, which will keep winds light and skies \nclear. Temperatures trend warmer each day this week, in the \nupper 50s to low 60s today, to upper 60s to near 70 by the end \nof the week. Clear skies and the dry airmass will allow for good\nradiational cooling each night, and lows will fall into the 30s\nareawide through at least Thursday. Moisture slowly starts to \nadvect into the region late in the work week and into the \nweekend, as a low pressure system starts to track northward \nalong the coast. Impacts to the area from this system will \nlikely remain minimal, mainly cloud cover and some rain showers \npossible Saturday and Sunday. At this time, does not look like \nheavy rain, as the moisture will have to overcome the dry \nairmass and stubborn high pressure. By the weekend, a 500mb \nshortwave tracks into the area from the west, bringing a cold \nfront towards the Appalachians, and finally pushing the high \noffshore, and increasing precipitation chances for the \nmountains.",
